ZS-05: armed mailbox register accesses (the driver of the A3000 + Z3660 kernel)

src/z3660.c of the amigaux/amix kernel/drivers/z3660scsi (ZS-05,
2026-10-26) with the dev_kvmap mapping of 518d246 kept: every mailbox
write is issued right after a read of an offset covering it, in one asm
block at IPL 7, and each address-triple cell is read back before the
doorbell (the Z3660 FPGA samples rising address bits of back-to-back
060 cycles too early and delivers a write at the AND of the two
addresses).  Also: before the fixed window's first signature write it
must lie outside the boot's memory regions and answer a read-only
bprobe (z3660_fixed_gate); a unit with no drive mapped answers INQUIRY
with peripheral qualifier 3, type 0x1F; the -DZ3660SCSI_MODULE form
(not built here).  This is commit e71d683 of the amix-z3660scsi
checkout (branch zs05-amigaux) that relink-040-z3660.sh compiles for
/stand/unix on the box (unix.z3-vt2 since 2026-11-04, m6-msp since
2026-11-08).

